a: Relationships (7569)]\"},{\"summary\":\"HER2 receptor testing from biopsy samples also drives treatment planning choices\",\"explanation\":\"HER2 receptors (including the expanded HER2 receptor entity) are described as measured/tested from biopsy samples to establish HER2 status, which affects breast cancer treatment decisions. [Data: Entities (3695, 3607)]\\n\\nRelationships support both the analytic step (biopsy sample tested for HER2 receptors to establish status) and the downstream consequence (treatment described as based on HER2 testing results). [Data: Relationships (7363, 7570)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Prostate biopsy evaluation is a specialized pathway focused on microscopic grading and risk estimation\",\"explanation\":\"PROSTATE BIOPSY EVALUATION is defined as the diagnostic assessment in which a biopsy sample is examined microscopically and graded using Gleason patterns combined into a Gleason score (interpreted via Grade Groups) to estimate aggressiveness and risk. [Data: Entities (3369, 406)]\\n\\nA direct relationship connects the biopsy sample to prostate biopsy evaluation, indicating the evaluation is performed on the biopsy sample to determine grading information. [Data: Relationships (6691)]\"},{\"summary\":\"The community is clinically oriented and decision-centric rather than adversarial or compliance-related\",\"explanation\":\"All entities and relationships describe routine clinical specimen collection (tumor biopsy producing a biopsy sample), laboratory testing (biomarker/receptor assessment), and clinical decision support (treatment planning based on receptor results). There are no references to illicit activity, security threats, or regulatory violations in the provided data. [Data: Entities (3822, 406, 5241); Relationships (7881, 11604)]\\n\\nThe explicit linkage of receptor testing outcomes to treatment planning indicates the core impact is medical: enabling selection of appropriate therapies based on tumor biology (HR status and HER2 status